  "distinctions": [
    "Torch lifecycle is a MINISTER/ACOLYTE event, never a PRIEST posture or source-text clock.",
    "The normal torch stop is after chalice elevation; keep torches to Communion if there are communicants, it is a fast day or it is a Requiem. When conditions overlap there is one actual extinguishing, not three separate events.",
    "The torch rule here is expressly for Solemn Mass; do not infer universal torches for Low or Missa Cantata, even with incense.",
    "The subdeacon genuflects in his place as separately prescribed in VIII.8; source does not justify manufacturing repeated genuflections for every paragraph.",
    "The existing 11 minister branches, including deacon, thurifer and the conditional pall, retain ownership; this supplemental table does not duplicate those events.",
    "Cues are research location hints. Scroll position does not demonstrate that minister, acolyte or priest actions have occurred."
